e Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "Walk termination moved from the link rule to every caller: three walkers each hand-roll a revisit guard, keyed two different ways", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: before this change the link rule ended every walk by construction ('strictly before' in store order). An anchor is now found by id anywhere in the store, so ending the walk became an obligation on each caller, and linked_reviews' docstring now says so ('every walker that loops over this link also refuses to revisit a fact'). Each of the three loops pays it separately: gates._review_verified_passes_stand_on keys a set on id(dict), plan_status._extended_reviews keys on id(dict), and critic_mode.review_chain keys on the fact-id string. That id()-versus-fact-id split is the drift the same docstring cites as its reason for having one owner ('identity by id() vs by fact id'). The consequence: a fourth walker written against prior_review/linked_reviews (the stated 'one owner') that misses a guard documented only in prose spins forever on a malformed store, inside the Stop hook. Close it by construction. Add one generator to coverage_algebra that yields the prior-link chain from a fact and owns the revisit guard under one identity rule, have the three walkers consume it, and add gates' walker to linked_reviews' consumer list, which leaves it out. Search for loops that call coverage_algebra.prior_review or linked_reviews more than once; expect only these three today. The refactor should not change what any walk reaches, so it is a dedup and not a reach change. Pin that with the existing cycle and order tests (test_a_cycle_of_passes_ends, test_review_chain_ends_at_an_anchor_already_on_it, test_the_extended_line_ends_on_a_cycle). If the builder judges a refactor at this boundary too costly, accept and file it.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/plan_status.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "scope": "class", "closure": "A loop that calls coverage_algebra.prior_review or linked_reviews repeatedly to walk a review's link and must therefore guard termination itself.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/lib/gates.py:_review_verified_passes_stand_on"}, {"id": "m2", "site": "plugin/lib/plan_status.py:_extended_reviews"}, {"id": "m3", "site": "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py:review_chain"}], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Governing-Artifact Reconciliation: nothing to reconcile", "recommendation": "No live plan claims fix/verify-links-review-id (the manifest's scope is unbound), and the change record has no governed_by dispositions, so no recorded disposition exists to test against the diff. record_lint's governed-by-gap count is 0. If this work had a plan, `prawduct-hook jurisdiction` would seed its governed_by. No edit wanted for this merge.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/verify-links-review-id.md"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Goal 1 probes: suite evidence current, coverage not required", "recommendation": "`prawduct-hook test-status` exits 0: tree-valid, recorded this session at 2026-11-23T21:41:12Z, and the working tree is identical to the recorded run (8ceb1cb51fd5, the dispatch tree). `verify-coverage` is skipped because coverage_required is false. Nothing to act on.", "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "The deferral's blocker condition now pays a gate composition on the SessionStart and inference paths", "recommendation": "critic_mode._gate_counts_an_open_blocker replaces a walk over the chain's facts with critic_consolidate.gate_counted_blockers. On a clone-wide store holding any unresolved blocker anywhere, that composes a coverage verdict from the merge-base. It is memoized through the verdict cache, because `read` is passed and `read['facts']` is the list composed, and the change record states it. So the change is intended and documented, and I found no correctness defect in it. The fallback to the chain when the gate returns None is tested both ways (TestTheDeferralAsksTheGatesCount). Noted so the added cost on these paths is visible. No edit wanted.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "gate_counted_blockers' docstring describes only verify-pass callers, and the deferral is now a caller at a different tree", "recommendation": "critic_consolidate.gate_counted_blockers says it answers 'at the verify pass's base_tree' and lists four callers that 'ask the gate identically'. critic_mode._gate_counts_an_open_blocker now calls it at the newest review's head_tree to decide the extension deferral. Nothing reads the prose, so it changes no behaviour. If the adapter's docstring is touched again, make it relational ('at the tree its caller names') rather than adding a fifth name to the list.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "missing_anchor re-checks base_tree separately from linked_reviews", "recommendation": "Two places decide that a pass with no usable base_tree links to nothing: the guard in linked_reviews and the one in missing_anchor. _resolve_claim already owns the other unresolved states. If it also returned 'unplaceable', both readers would ask one function. This is small and localized, and no change is wanted now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "The deferral's fallback to the chain when the gate cannot compose leaves no trace", "recommendation": "critic_mode._gate_counts_an_open_blocker quietly switches from the gate's composed count to the chain's own blockers when gate_counted_blockers returns None. Both arms err in the documented direction, so nobody takes a wrong action. But when someone asks why a deferral was or was not offered, nothing shows which arm decided. If the deferral line ever needs debugging, say which source decided in its reason text. No edit is wanted now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "Records Pass: data-model.md's `verifies` entry lists one unresolved case out of four", "recommendation": "The entry says that a `verifies` naming a review this store lacks links to none. A mismatched anchor head_tree, a value not shaped like a review id, and a pass with no usable base_tree also link to none (coverage_algebra._resolve_claim, linked_reviews). The change record states all four, and the entry's safe-direction summary is still true. It ships nothing and misleads no one into action, so it clears no Records Pass bar and no edit is wanted.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md"], "oid": "O-7"}], "duration_seconds": 540, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/verify-links-review-id`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {}, "base_reviewed": "ccc5a1d450a6b5a7a1dc9d9786f903d2cfd51930", "record_lint": {"records": [".claude/rules/learnings/reviews.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/verify-links-review-id.md", "documentation/issues/1160-design.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0, "late-requirement-record": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "base-moved", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-23T21:43:18Z